<Base
  title="Privacy — labs.walerys.app"
  description="How this personal Labs site handles hosting requests, theme preferences, and privacy questions."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1 id="privacy">Privacy</h1>
    <p>Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-23">23 October 2026</time></p>

    <h2 id="this-site">This site</h2>
    <p>
      I’m Leszek Walerys, the operator of Labs, a personal static blog about software,
      hardware, and experiments. This notice explains what happens when you browse
      the site and how to reach me about privacy.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site currently has no user accounts, comments, contact forms, newsletter,
      analytics, advertising, or tracking widgets. It does not embed third-party
      content or load third-party fonts. Browsing does not automatically contact
      LinkedIn. This does not mean that no personal data is processed: delivering
      pages involves requests to the hosting service.
    </p>

    <h2 id="hosting">Hosting and request data</h2>
    <p>
      GitHub Pages hosts this site and receives the request data needed to serve its
      pages. GitHub states that visitors’ IP addresses are logged and stored for
      security purposes, whether or not visitors are signed into GitHub. See the
      official <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages#data-collection">GitHub Pages data collection documentation</a>{' '}
      and the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>{' '}
      for details about GitHub’s own processing and privacy practices.
    </p>

    <h2 id="theme-storage">Theme preference</h2>
    <p>
      The default theme is dark. Only after you explicitly choose a theme does the
      site save <code>light</code> or <code>dark</code> under the key <code>theme</code>{' '}
      in your browser’s <code>sessionStorage</code>. On subsequent page loads, it
      reads that preference without writing a new value automatically.
    </p>
    <p>
      This preference lasts for the browser tab’s session, rather than being a
      permanent preference across visits. You can remove it using your browser’s
      site-storage controls. It is not a cookie or a visitor identifier, and the
      site’s code does not transmit it to a server.
    </p>
    <p>
      There is currently no consent popup because the site does not use
      nonessential tracking. This describes the current implementation, not a
      general claim that every site or storage use is exempt from consent rules.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact-and-rights">Contact and privacy rights</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy questions or to ask about any rights that apply to your personal
      data, contact me through my{' '}
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/leszekwalerys/">LinkedIn profile</a>.
      Messaging availability depends on your LinkedIn account and settings.
      This is an ordinary external link: following it leaves this site and hands
      navigation over to LinkedIn, whose own privacy policy applies there.
      Questions about GitHub’s own processing can also be directed to GitHub
      through the contact and rights information in its privacy statement.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
